.TH CHESS 1
.SH NAME
chess \- chess diagrams for troff
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chess
[
.I file ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Chess
is a preprocessor for
.IR troff (1),
as
.IR pic (1)
is: it copies the
.IR file s,
or its standard input, to its standard output, setting each board
between
.B .CB
and
.B .CE
as a diagram.
A board is a position in Forsyth-Edwards notation and, if wanted, how
it is to be set, a setting a line:
.TP
.BI fen " position " \fR[\fPw \fR|\fP b\fR]\fP
The position: its ranks from the eighth, separated by
.BR / ,
in each its pieces from the a-file
.RB ( KQRBNP
White's,
.B kqrbnp
Black's), a digit for empty squares; then who is to move.
.TP
.BI size " n"
The board's side, in inches (2).
.TP
.B flip
Black at the foot.
.TP
.B nocoords
The files and ranks not named.
.PP
Its dark squares are grey, its pieces the Unicode chess figures of
the font
.B CH
(Noto Sans Symbols 2's), a white piece filled white, and the files and
ranks named along its edges.
A board is written as
.I pic
writes a picture
.RB ( .PS
.I "height width" ,
its drawing,
.BR .PE ),
so that the macros place it as one:
.B -mbook
centres it, keeps it on one page and, in a tagged PDF, makes it a
.BR Figure ,
described by
.B .alt
or, with none, by the position read out
(\(lqChess diagram. White: King e1, ...\(rq).
.PP
Moves in the text are set in figurine notation as written,
.B ♘f3
or
.BR ♕xb7 :
.B -mbook
mounts
.B CH
as a special font, so its figures are found from any font.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\&.CB
fen 1n1Rkb1r/p4ppp/4q3/4p1B1/4P3/8/PPP2PPP/2K5 b
\&.CE
.EE
.PP
Morphy's mate of 1858, in a book:
.B book
runs
.I chess
when the book has a
.BR .CB .
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/chess.b
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
A position that is not eight ranks of eight squares, an unknown
piece or setting, or a board with no
.B fen
or no
.BR .CE ,
is said with its file and line, and
.I chess
fails at the end.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR book (1),
.IR pic (1),
.IR troff (1)
